  "info": {
    "title": "PlaneMem Canonical CloudEvent v1 message catalog",
    "version": "0.1.0",
    "description": "Source-only reusable structured JSON message components for all 38 default v1 CanonicalEvent types. Each payload is the entire CloudEvents 1.0 profile object, including the complete CanonicalEvent in data. Typed anchors pair outer type with data.event_type. This catalog declares no server, channel, operation, protocol binding or delivery guarantee. Validation, generation and runtime compatibility have not been executed."
  },
  "defaultContentType": "application/cloudevents+json",
  "x-todo": "P0-01",
  "x-scope": "reusable-structured-message-catalog-only",
  "x-canonical-schema-version": 1,
  "x-cloudevents-specversion": "1.0",
  "x-schema-loading": "Load ../schemas/canonical-cloudevent-v1-catalog.json and all six sibling event schemas locally with their $id mappings. Do not fetch planemem.local. A consumer must explicitly support JSON Schema 2020-12 in Multi Format Schema payloads; this format is not assumed to be every AsyncAPI tool's default.",
  "x-runtime-boundaries": [
    "Use toCanonicalCloudEvent and fromCanonicalCloudEvent with an explicit source; schema acceptance does not authenticate a producer or grant scope/sensitivity permissions.",
    "The complete structured payload uses application/cloudevents+json; its data is a complete CanonicalEvent with datacontenttype application/json, not an encoded JSON string.",
    "The source/id pair is the CloudEvents duplicate identity. This catalog does not add persistence or change the legacy event_id-only ledger.",
    "Both outer type and data.event_type are constrained together for each message; id/time/subject equality, expected source, URI/calendar/scalar-string validity and complete 1 MiB/depth/node bounds still require the adapter.",
    "The closed profile does not accept arbitrary extensions, data_base64, binary/batch formats or custom registry types/versions.",
    "Most business payloads remain open objects. Deletion/restoration structures are retained; business effects, restore arithmetic, ordering/retries and broker acknowledgement remain consumer responsibilities."
  ],
